---- what the field did, with nobody in the room ----
  dark baseline      n= 22       3 - 11     median    8.5
  lit, empty room    n= 15      66 - 68     median   67.0
  dark again         n= 20       4 - 10     median    7.0
  dim 20%            n= 16      21 - 26     median   23.0
  dim 100%           n= 11      67 - 68     median   67.0

  at switch-on: +59.5 counts over dark.  two minutes later, still lit: +58.5.  back in the dark: -1.5.

---- verdict ----
  IT IS THE LOAD. 0x13 held +58.5 counts above dark after two minutes lit, in an empty
  room, and fell back to -1.5 when the lamp went off. Nobody was near the sensor at any
  point, so a finger in front of the PIR cannot explain it. The load-detector reading stands,
  and so does the feedback-loop worry: this baseline is what a walk-past has to rise above.

  AND IT TRACKS BRIGHTNESS: 20% sits at 23.0, 100% at 67.0 (+44.0). The
  baseline moves with the dim level, not just with on/off -- which the bridge does not re-learn.

---- what the BRIDGE made of it (a separate question) ----
  It reported motion 5x with nobody there. Each one would light a room, restamp
  motion_at, and hold an `idle` rule off for as long as it lasts.
    +  15.9s   during: dark baseline
    +  40.0s   during: dark baseline
    + 304.6s   during: dark again
    + 407.2s   during: dim 20%
    + 430.2s   during: between windows (settling)

  At least one landed in a dim leg. A Level Status does not re-learn the floor (only the
  0x8204 branch does), so a brightness change is the case that latches. That is the bug.
